From: startergo <https://github.com/startergo/homebrew-qemu-virgl-kosmickrisp>
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: clear the GL dirty flag once the render completes

Vendored from homebrew-qemu-virgl-kosmickrisp commit
cbfb7641c933e8364dda0a035830603fd7455a4e, patches/gpu-spike-resolution-fix.patch.
That tree has been unmaintained since 2026-01-14 and this was the last file
Try Omarchy still consumed from it, so it is carried here rather than
downloading the whole archive for one small patch.

Fixed while vendoring: the upstream patch moved the gl_dirty clear out of
cocoa_gl_refresh and into cocoa_gl_render, but indented it inside the
"if (cocoa_gl_trace_enabled())" block, so the flag was only ever cleared when
GL tracing was switched on. In a normal build gl_dirty latched true on the
first damage and stayed true, and cocoa_gl_refresh then re-rendered the
scanout on every refresh tick for the life of the VM. The clear now sits at
function scope, which is what the comment describes and what the code it
replaced in cocoa_gl_refresh did.

Applies after the texture-borrowing patch.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -2337,6 +2337,9 @@
         glFlush();
         cocoa_gl_log_error("render end");
     }
+
+    /* Clear dirty flag after render completes to ensure clean handoff */
+    gl_dirty = false;
 }
 
 static void cocoa_gl_refresh(DisplayChangeListener *dcl)
@@ -2344,7 +2347,6 @@
     cocoa_refresh(dcl);
 
     if (gl_dirty) {
-        gl_dirty = false;
 
         if (cocoa_gl_trace_enabled()) {
             cocoa_gl_log("refresh: triggering render dirty scanout=%d egl_surface=%d",
